    "updated_at": "2017-05-16T12:46:36Z",
    "body": "That actually is \"resize topLevelDoc’s viewport to its 'normal' dimensions\" from \"exit fullscreen\".\r\n\r\nActually, it seems to me we need a \"resize\" variable in `requestFullscreen` algorithm as well, and do the resizing only when that is true, and we can call \"resize ... to its 'normal' dimensions\" when error happens in the \"next animation frame task\" and resize is true.",
